{{!--
  Override of the nav-tree partial of ui-bundle.zip (the original is unchanged except for the marked lines).
  It emits only the levels a reader needs, so the nav does not repeat the whole subtree of every section in every
  page (that made guide pages over 1 MB). The child list of an entry is rendered only when
    - the entry is at a depth up to site.keys.nav_expand_depth (default 1: the groups and the sections are listed), or
    - it contains the current page, or
    - its parent opened its children (an untitled list wrapper at depth 0, or a group titled in the comma-separated
      site.keys.nav_open_groups, default none), or
    - it is a text-only group heading (children and no url): it has no page of its own, so its children are always
      emitted, with a toggle, collapsed unless it is on the path to the current page.
  The two playbook keys are written in snake_case in the playbook and read here in camelCase, because Antora camelCases
  the keys of `site.keys` (navOpenGroups, navExpandDepth).
  All of this is computed once per entry by the nav-item-state helper (helpers/nav-item-state.js).
  Pruned entries always have a url: readers reach their subtree through the entry's own link (its index page), so
  never prune an entry that has no url. Other subtrees are not in the HTML (and get no toggle button).
  The bundle's toggle buttons and the "toggle all" button keep working because they only toggle the is-active class that
  is rendered here. The entries on the path to the current page are rendered with is-active, so the ancestors of the
  current page are open.
  The marker comment inside every list lets scripts/site-metrics/measure.mjs tell this override from the bundle's
  own partial (both write data-depth).
  With the defaults and a small nav this renders the same as the bundle, so the override is safe on any site.
--}}
{{#if navigation.length}}
<ul class="nav-list">
  <!-- nav-tree override -->
  {{#each navigation as |item|}}
  {{!-- open and expand state computed once per entry (see the header comment and the helper) --}}
  {{#with (nav-item-state item ../level ../open @root.page.url @root.site.keys.navOpenGroups @root.site.keys.navExpandDepth) as |s|}}
  <li class="nav-item{{#if s.current}} is-current-page{{/if}}{{#if s.active}} is-active{{/if}}" data-depth="{{s.depth}}">
    {{#if item.content}}
    {{#if s.toggle}}
    <button class="nav-item-toggle"></button>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if item.url}}
    <a class="nav-link" href="
      {{~#if (eq item.urlType 'internal')}}{{{relativize item.url}}}
      {{~else}}{{{item.url}}}{{~/if}}">{{{item.content}}}</a>
    {{else}}
    <span class="nav-text">{{{item.content}}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    {{/if}}
{{!-- emit the child list only when needed; an untitled wrapper and the groups in nav_open_groups open their children --}}
{{#if s.expand}}
{{> nav-tree navigation=item.items level=s.childLevel open=s.openChildren}}
{{/if}}
  </li>
  {{/with}}
  {{/each}}
</ul>
{{/if}}
